 75NI    COULOMB EXCITATION:XUNDL-3    2020GO06                           202010
 75NI c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2020Go06:                          
 75NI2c  Phys Rev C 102, 014323 (2020)                                          
 75NI c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster), September 14, 2020                    
 75NI c  2020Go06: beam={+75}Ni with an average energy of 215 MeV/nucleon.      
 75NI2c  Target was 1.177 g/cm{+2} thick natural Pb. {+75}Ni beam from          
 75NI3c  {+9}Be({+238}U,F),E=345 MeV/nucleon primary reaction. Fragments were   
 75NI4c  identified in Z and A/Q by B|r-|DE-B|r and time-of-flight techniques   
 75NI5c  using the BigRIPS fragment separator at RIBF-RIKEN facility. Reaction  
 75NI6c  products after Coulomb excitation were identified by the ZeroDegree    
 75NI7c  spectrometer, and finally transported to the WAS3Abi-EURICA counting   
 75NI8c  setup. Measured scattered {+75}Ni ions by the WAS3Abi counting system, 
 75NI9c  E|g, I|g, (particle)|g-coin using the DALI2 array of 186 NaI(Tl)       
 75NIAc  scintillators for |g detection. Deduced excitation cross sections      
 75NIBc  and yields for the excited states, and B(E2) using FRESCO computer     
 75NICc  code. Comparison with large-scale shell-model calculations using the   
 75NIDc  Cd-Bonn potential and two model spaces: 1. f{-7/2}, p{-3/2}, f{-5/2},  
 75NIEc  p{-1/2}, g{-9/2} and d{-5/2} orbitals for neutrons and protons;        
 75NIFc  2. protons in the f{-7/2}, p{-3/2} and f{-5/2} orbitals, and neutrons  
 75NIGc  in the p{-3/2}, f{-5/2}, p{-1/2} and g{-9/2} orbitals.                 
 75NI c  Compiler's note: beam energy of 215 MeV/nucleon for {+75}Ni is not     
 75NI2c  explicitly specified by 2020Go06, assumed here the same as listed by   
 75NI3c  authors for {+74}Ni                                                    
 75NI cG $B(E2) values are listed here in e{+2}b{+2} units. Authors, in their   
 75NI2cG Table II, listed the values in e{+2}fm{+4} units.                      
 75NI cL E(A)$Tentative level.                                                  
 75NI cL J$As proposed by 2020Go06, based on predictions                        
 75NI2cL by shell-model calculations that these are members of the |ng{-9/2}{+n}
 75NI3cL multiplet. The assignments are tentative.                              
